  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-05-30T04:48:00.217Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "This is a minor improvement for incorrect inputs, but currently if you put a link to a YouTube video that includes a playlist in the link into a video player, the link resolution will take much longer than it should. This is because YouTubeDL will go through the entire playlist and resolve each video's link needlessly since we can only retrieve the first video in VRC. \nAdding `--no-playlist` to the YTDL invocation makes it skip the playlist and only grab the video the user has input. It also seems like `--no-playlist` is currently stripped from VRC's version of YTDL so it'd need to be added there too.",
